  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Decentralisering och &#xe5;terh&#xe4;mtning i Ukraina 2024-2028</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Decentralization and Recovery in Ukraine 2024-2028</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Syftet med programmet &#xe4;r att ytterligare st&#xf6;dja decentraliseringsprocessen i Ukraina genom ett l&#xe5;ngsiktigt fokus p&#xe5; att &#xe5;tg&#xe4;rda inkonsekvenserna i Ukrainas lokala sj&#xe4;lvstyresystem och flerniv&#xe5;styre och samtidigt st&#xe4;rka kommunernas tillhandah&#xe5;llande av offentliga tj&#xe4;nster, samt deras direkta engagemang i &#xe5;terh&#xe4;mtnings- och &#xe5;teruppbyggnadsprocessen, i linje med kraven f&#xf6;r EU-anslutning.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The aim of the programme is to support further the decentralization process in Ukraine through a long term focus on addressing the inconsistencies in Ukraine&apos;s local self-government framework and system of multi-level governance and in parallel strengthening municipalities&apos; public service provision, as well as their direct engagement in the recovery and reconstruction process, in line with the requirements of EU accession.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The proposed programme aims to address the inconsistencies in Ukraine&apos;s local self government (LSG) framework and system of multilevel governance while
strengthening municipalities public service provision, as well as their direct engagement in the recovery and reconstruction process, in line with the requirements of EU integration. To address urgent needs caused by the war, while simultaneously building long term capacities and consolidating and
strengthening the decentralisation process in Ukraine, the project is designed as a two-component programme, covering five thematic areas in which Sweden
and SALAR has unique experience and credibility in Ukraine.

Component 1: Multilevel governance and policy

Component 2: Enhancing the capacity of municipalities

Thematic Areas: Education, Administrative Service Provision, Fiscal Decentralisation, Locally Led Recovery and International Municipal Cooperation.</narrative>
  </description>
